      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the range of the set of numbers, we need to determine the largest number in the set.\n\nThe mean of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by the total number of numbers. In this case, we have a set with two additional numbers, so the mean of the set is:\n\n4 = (1 + (unknown number) + (largest number)) / 3\n\nThere is not enough information to find the largest number directly. However, since the mean of the numbers is 4, the sum of the three numbers must be 12.\n\nWe know that the smallest number is 1, so let's call the unknown number x and the largest number y. We can set up the following equation:\n\n4 = (1 + x + y) / 3\n\nMultiplying both sides by 3, we get:\n\n4 * 3 = 1 + x + y\n12 = 1 + x + y\n\nNow we can solve for x + y:\n\n12 - 1 = 1 + x + y - 1\n11 = x + y\n\nSince we are looking for the range, which is the difference between the largest and smallest numbers, we know that y must be greater than 1:\n\ny > 1\n\nHowever, we cannot determine an exact range for the numbers without more information.",
